E AX3142 initializer-captured.ax:9:50-56 field-effect-exceeded "the lambda performs IO, and the field `Hook.run` declares `effect(pure)`" #"performs IO" !"a call through `Hook.run` is charged what the field declares and nothing else, so everything stored in it has to keep that" ?"store a function that keeps the declaration, or declare the effect on the field with `;@axiom:effect(io)`"
E AX3042 initializer-captured.ax:9:10-15 undeclared-effect "`build` performs IO and its declaration does not say so" !"effects are INFERRED transitively, so this fires on every function up the call chain, and each one is a place a reader would otherwise have to open the callee to learn it. If the effect is not wanted here the fix is to stop performing it, not to stop saying so. `IO`, `Entropy`, `Spawn` and `Block` are required; `Alloc` and `Mut` are ambient and never need declaring" ?9:1:"write `;@axiom:effect(io)` above the declaration"~>";@axiom:effect(io)\n"
E AX3143 initializer-parameter.ax:9:31-37 field-effect-unknown "the compiler can't show that the value stored in `Hook.run` keeps `effect(pure)`: it is a lambda that calls the parameter `f`, which each caller chooses" #"effects unknown here" !"a call through `Hook.run` is charged what the field declares and nothing else, so a value whose effects can't be determined is refused rather than trusted" ?"store a named function or a lambda whose body the compiler can see, or build the record where the function is known"
E AX3143 initializer-mutable.ax:9:54-60 field-effect-unknown "the compiler can't show that the value stored in `Hook.run` keeps `effect(pure)`: it is the lambda, which calls a value the compiler could not resolve, so its effects are a lower bound" #"effects unknown here" !"a call through `Hook.run` is charged what the field declares and nothing else, so a value whose effects can't be determined is refused rather than trusted" ?"store a named function or a lambda whose body the compiler can see, or build the record where the function is known"
