E AX3042 initializer-alias.ax:9:10-15 undeclared-effect "`build` performs IO and its declaration does not say so" !"effects are INFERRED transitively, so this fires on every function up the call chain, and each one is a place a reader would otherwise have to open the callee to learn it. If the effect is not wanted here the fix is to stop performing it, not to stop saying so. `IO`, `Entropy`, `Spawn` and `Block` are required; `Alloc` and `Mut` are ambient and never need declaring" ?9:1:"write `;@axiom:effect(io)` above the declaration"~>";@axiom:effect(io)\n"
E AX3070 480-field-on-mixed-data.ax:17:7-8 unsafe-field-access "field access `.v` is unsafe on `T`: the type has a nullary constructor, so a value may be an immediate tag with no fields to read" #"the value may not be a block at all" !"an unguarded load on an immediate dereferences a small integer: this passed `check` and died of SIGSEGV (docs/memory-model.md MM-VAL-9a)" ?"match on the value instead, and read the field in the fieldful arm - a `match` emits the immediate-or-address guard that field access cannot"
E AX3070 484-field-on-partial-data.ax:16:5-6 unsafe-field-access "field access `.r` is unsafe on `Shape`: not every constructor declares that field, so a value built by another constructor has no such word to read" #"only some constructors declare this field" !"an unguarded load on a value of another constructor reads its slot, or a word past its block: this passed `check` and died of SIGSEGV" ?"match on the value instead, and read the field in the arm that has it - a `match` emits the tag guard that field access cannot"
